<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Petroz seeks compensation over claim.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Petroz seeks compensation over claim.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petroz NL said on Wednesday it has filed legal compensation proceedings against the Commonwealth of Australia over the loss of its interest in WA-74-P exploration permit offshore of Western Australia.</p>
<p>The permit was redefined as a result of amendments to the Petroleum Australia-Indonesia Zone of Cooperation Act of 1990 causing permit holders to lose their interest in part of the permit area, Pertroz said.</p>
<p>At that time, the interests in WA-74-P were held 55.625 percent by Petroz, 20 percent by Pontoon NL, 16.25 percent by WMC Ltd 16.25 percent and 18.125 percent by Laist Pty Ltd (8.125 percent).</p>
<p>WMC has previously instituted proceedings against the Commonwealth, seeking compensation for the loss of its interests, Petroz said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
